{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge","id":1169462,"title":"Mages and 2e Fae/Hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-21T13:50:13-08:00","id":1169462,"title":"Mages and 2e Fae/Hedge","content":"Okay now that we know what Changeling looks like, how do you think Mages will interact with all things Fae? <br /> <br /> Can mages have Hedge Ghost Familiars?<br /> <br /> Can a Mage with time and fate retroactively cause someone to become Fae Touched by creating a meaningful oath between the would be Avowed and a Changeling? <br /> <br /> Can Mages open gateways to the Hedge? <br /> <br /> Can a dreaming Mage interact with Eidolons? <br /> <br /> It turns out any Emphereal being manifests physically in the Hedge, so I guess visiting Goetic Familiars can manifest there as if they we're in the Astral. <br /> <br /> How do you think the Drain Numina works when used on Essence Emphereals by Glamour based Emphereals and vis versa?<br /> <br /> Can Mages collect Glamour the way they do essence.<br /> <br /> And how far would a Mage go to possess the Crown of Thorns if he knew about it?<br /> <br /> What would an Archmages Eidolons look like?<br /> <br /> Could there be Abyssal Hedge Ghosts?<br /> <br /> Can Mages get the Hedge Denizen &amp; Goblin Queen Condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T14:27:02-08:00","id":1169474,"title":"","content":"Probably not.<br /> <br /> Maybe.<br /> <br /> Probably not.<br /> <br /> Probably, assuming they know to look for them.<br /> <br /> It probably continues to work just fine, but an essence dependent entity is unlikely to be able to use any glamour it drains and vice versa. Incidentally, it\u2019s my understanding that entities from the Hedge are not ephemeral entities though they use the same rules. This is similar to Supernal (and many Abyssal) entities which also aren\u2019t ephemeral.<br /> <br /> They probably can if they\u2019re aware it exists, possibly with Fate.<br /> <br /> No idea.<br /> <br /> No idea.<br /> <br /> There can be Abyssal anything.<br /> <br /> Probably not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T15:20:24-08:00","id":1169497,"title":"","content":"As to the last one, hedge denizen does call out that it can be gained by any mortal or non-changelings supernatural. I just think that the hedge queen has further requirements but I'm not certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T15:42:57-08:00","id":1169502,"title":"","content":"Here's a different set of answers, since most of the questions are up to house ruling.<br /> <br /> Maybe.<br /> <br /> Probably.<br /> <br /> Fate 3 for Open Hedge Gate and Fate 5 for Create Hedge Gate, as stated by Dave Brookshaw.<br /> <br /> Eidolons might just be the kind of Goetia that mages call dream actors, only the book uses a different system because it doesn't reprint the regular ephemeral system. In that case definitely. Otherwise; probably.<br /> <br /> The Hedge doesn't have Twilight so all ephemeral entities just skip Twilight Form and are as if they're Materialized. The same thing happens in the Shadow, the Underworld and the Astral.<br /> <br /> Not sure. It might work, or it might require a similar Numen to transform between energy types.<br /> <br /> Probably, but I'm not sure which Arcanum would be right. It's fae magic, but it's also emotions in the form of supernatural energy. Fate and/or Mind could be it.<br /> <br /> If the mage also knows about all the drawbacks; probably not that far. Only Banish is something that would be difficult to recreate with Supernal magic, and there's other ways to get rid of someone.<br /> <br /> No idea. I'm honestly not sure where the eidolons/bastions of Changeling fit in with the Goetia of the Astral Plane from Mage. As far as I can tell the dreams that Changelings can enter should be the first of the four Astral Realms; the personal dream plane. They're just described differently, and the concept of a Bastion is completely absent from what I've read in Mage. (But I haven't read much of the first edition, to be honest.)<br /> <br /> It's the Abyss. I'm almost sure it's required to have abyssal hedge ghosts.<br /> <br /> Maybe. Maybe not. A &quot;fun&quot; Mystery to explore!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T16:04:44-08:00","id":1169511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay now that we know what Changeling looks like, how do you think Mages will interact with all things Fae?<br /> <br /> Can mages have Hedge Ghost Familiars?</div> </div> </div> </div> In theory, mages can do anything. Its all a matter of getting the research and experiments in. And ST approval.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a Mage with time and fate retroactively cause someone to become Fae Touched by creating a meaningful oath between the would be Avowed and a Changeling? </div> </div> </div> Yes, they can use Time to Rewrite history and lead to someone making different choices to become fae touched. Cue disclaimer on all temporal shinanigans expiring, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Mages open gateways to the Hedge? </div> </div> </div> Yes. Open, close, into the hedge, out of the hedge, create their own gateways at Fate 5 going either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a dreaming Mage interact with Eidolons? </div> </div> </div> Good chance that eidolons are just your goetic vices and your super ego. Mages are better at interacting with them through the astral than changelings are. And mind mages can enter dreams as well as a changeling can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It turns out any Emphereal being manifests physically in the Hedge, so I guess visiting Goetic Familiars can manifest there as if they we're in the Astral. </div> </div> </div> Maybe. They could just go intangible like hedge ghosts. Goetics are funny that way, because, storywise, they're not supposed to ever be able to Materialize without some physical body to possess, or be transformed by a Patterning spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you think the Drain Numina works when used on Essence Emphereals by Glamour based Emphereals and vis versa? </div> </div> </div> There are no glamour-based ephemerals. Hedge ghosts aren't in twilight (even when Ironside), aren't made of ephemeral. Drain Numina targets material beings in the first place, though, no way to target a hedge ghost. Targeting a fae creature will drain willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Mages collect Glamour the way they do essence. </div> </div> </div> See first answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And how far would a Mage go to possess the Crown of Thorns if he knew about it? </div> </div> </div> As something to study for their Obsession? Almost any length. As a tool to use? Very little.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would an Archmages Eidolons look like? </div> </div> </div> Same as any other former human's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could there be Abyssal Hedge Ghosts? </div> </div> </div> Anything is possible. That said, they won't be showing up the same way an acamoth or golmoth would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Mages get the Hedge Denizen &amp; Goblin Queen Condition? </div> </div> </div> In theory, anything is possible. Not very likely, but possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-21-2017, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T17:06:45-08:00","id":1169526,"title":"","content":"All these answers and more should be revealed in The Contagion Chronicle crossover book. Coming Soon(tm) ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T17:43:02-08:00","id":1169536,"title":"","content":"I seriously doubt that. Some of these, maybe, but if the goal of the Contagion Chronicle is to answer questions at this level then there wouldn't be any room left for exploring the eponymous Contagion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T18:47:51-08:00","id":1169550,"title":"","content":"Even if the Contagion Chronicles do answer this, most likely we\u2019ll get something similar in scale to the Mage-Mummy interaction rules we got in Dark Eras Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T17:33:31-08:00","id":1169783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge?p=1169526#post1169526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All these answers and more should be revealed in The Contagion Chronicle crossover book. Coming Soon(tm) ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Contagion Chronicles will be no where close to being soon, think 2020 at the earliest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T17:49:14-08:00","id":1169786,"title":"","content":"&quot;Soon(tm)&quot; is a sarcastic way of saying it'll take quite some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T18:18:23-08:00","id":1169789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge?p=1169786#post1169786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Soon(tm)&amp;quot; is a sarcastic way of saying it'll take quite some time.</div> </div> </div> </div> Did not know that, oops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T22:07:52-08:00","id":1170372,"title":"","content":"Reread Hedge Denizen and it's clear it applies to none Changelings and humans. <br /> <br /> So yes to answer my own question a nosy mage could easily find themselves a Hedge Denizen (hobgoblin). <br /> <br /> But it's also possible for an Acamoth or Gulmoth to end up with the Hedge Denizen condition, so that answers the question can their be Abyssal fae. <br /> <br /> If you familiar makes deals with hobgoblins to incur goblin debt it could also end up a hobgoblin. <br /> <br /> Really funny thought, but a Superneral Fae (instead of a Hedge/Arcadian fae) could end up with the condition under strange circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T22:52:58-08:00","id":1170378,"title":"","content":"A goblin mage sound absolutely terrifying, no less one who has a command of Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T09:45:53-08:00","id":1174049,"title":"","content":"These are all based on ST fiat in my opinion, so I had some fun with them. Here's a very pro-changeling take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay now that we know what Changeling looks like, how do you think Mages will interact with all things Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Poorly in my games, though to be fair I have a policy of &quot;If it can be interpreted to be a disadvantagous to a Mage, it is&quot; on all supernatural interactions.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can mages have Hedge Ghost Familiars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can't even enter the Hedge without risking losing everything so... no.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Mage with time and fate retroactively cause someone to become Fae Touched by creating a meaningful oath between the would be Avowed and a Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>A sufficiently powerful mage can attempt to do this, but it might not work out how they intend.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mages open gateways to the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, surviving entry long is another matter.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a dreaming Mage interact with Eidolons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It turns out any Emphereal being manifests physically in the Hedge, so I guess visiting Goetic Familiars can manifest there as if they we're in the Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. They're a good chance they'll be immediately destroyed with the wrong step though since they're soul-constructs.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you think the Drain Numina works when used on Essence Emphereals by Glamour based Emphereals and vis versa?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just rule it doesn't.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mages collect Glamour the way they do essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how far would a Mage go to possess the Crown of Thorns if he knew about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>As with any other obsession.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would an Archmages Eidolons look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume much less impressive than you'd hope.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could there be Abyssal Hedge Ghosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. There is no abyssal anything in the Hedge.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge#post1169462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mages get the Hedge Denizen &amp; Goblin Queen Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, a mage who so much as attempts to stroll down a road in the hedge is likely to lose all their magic forever. So... yeah.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge?p=1170378#post1170378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A goblin mage sound absolutely terrifying, no less one who has a command of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just like the basic description of a low-tier True Fae imo, so... yeah I guess terrifying but not particularly <i>special</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","user":"Knit-I-Fine","date":". 01-07-2018, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T14:23:57-08:00","id":1174982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge?p=1174049#post1174049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are all based on ST fiat in my opinion, so I had some fun with them. Here's a very pro-changeling take.</div> </div> </div> </div>...that violates canon.<br /> <br /> Seriously, there's a monster entry for mages who confuse Supernal Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia in <i>Dancers in the Dusk,</i> and get turned into hobgoblins by the Keepers for their trouble. It outright says that mages keep their powers until they get soul-mutilated by Gentry.<br /> <br /> Besides, these answers are <i>boring</i>, not a single plot hook among them. So, my pro-changeling answers:<br /> <br /> Okay now that we know what Changeling looks like, how do you think Mages will interact with all things Fae? <br /> <br /> <b>As with anything else: prodding it with a stick and seeing what Arcane Experience falls out.</b><br /> <br /> Can mages have Hedge Ghost Familiars?<br /> <br /> <b>They'd have to meet first, but with the proper Fate and/or Death spell, nothing insurmountable.</b><br /> <br /> Can a Mage with time and fate retroactively cause someone to become Fae Touched by creating a meaningful oath between the would be Avowed and a Changeling? <br /> <br /> <b>Yes, but it'd result in some major temporal paradox. And Paradox. That's a guy's life you're remaking there and messing with the Hedge in the process!</b><br /> <br /> Can Mages open gateways to the Hedge? <br /> <br /> <b>No, but they can figure out the key with it.</b><br /> <br /> Can a dreaming Mage interact with Eidolons? <br /> <br /> <b>Those are parts of a dreaming mind, so yeah.</b><br /> <br /> It turns out any Emphereal being manifests physically in the Hedge, so I guess visiting Goetic Familiars can manifest there as if they we're in the Astral. <br /> <br /> <b>Yes, but it's common for them to become Hedge Ghosts. They are already free-floating bits of soul and emotion after all, becoming bits adapted to the Hedge isn't hard.</b><br /> <br /> How do you think the Drain Numina works when used on Essence Emphereals by Glamour based Emphereals and vis versa?<br /> <br /> <b>Different fuels, different Numen needed. A spirit able to do that is a half-goblin magath, and a ghost able to has gone native.</b><br /> <br /> Can Mages collect Glamour the way they do essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Yep, though they need Fate to keep it stable and can't really use it without conversion to Mana or as bribes.</b><br /> <br /> And how far would a Mage go to possess the Crown of Thorns if he knew about it?<br /> <br /> <b>Depends on the mage.</b><br /> <br /> What would an Archmages Eidolons look like?<br /> <br /> <b>Not that different from normal eidolons. They dream like everyone else, it's just a more powerful mind dreaming.</b><br /> <br /> Could there be Abyssal Hedge Ghosts?<br /> <br /> <b>The Abyss is everything and nothing. How it got into the Hedge is anyone's guess, but it's hardly impossible; if there can be Abyssal Goetia, there can be Abyssal Hedge Ghosts (maybe it wasn't a good idea for retroactive Fae-Touched..).</b><br /> <br /> Can Mages get the Hedge Denizen &amp; Goblin Queen Condition?<br /> <br /> <b>On purpose, with the proper Legacy to get around that &quot;goblins won't sell to me&quot; issue. It's not worth it. Interesting method of lichdom, though.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T12:30:20-08:00","id":1175819,"title":"","content":"I've read nothing that suggests Hobgoblins won't make deals with Mages. Heck I see no reason why they won't make deals with Abyssal entities, which means say an Abyssal Ghost could end up with the condition and be a Hobgoblin. <br /> <br /> Here is a new question could Fate be used to cancel or transfer to another person Goblin Debt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T12:42:53-08:00","id":1175824,"title":"","content":"I think the bigger question is if mages have the sort of infrastructure that allows them to accrue Goblin Debt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T13:50:47-08:00","id":1175836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge?p=1175824#post1175824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the bigger question is if mages have the sort of infrastructure that allows them to accrue Goblin Debt.</div> </div> </div> </div>A 'Yes' is more interesting than a 'No' here, so absent any Word of God to the contrary, I feel like that's what we should roll with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T10:14:23-08:00","id":1175996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1169462-mages-and-2e-fae-hedge?p=1175824#post1175824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the bigger question is if mages have the sort of infrastructure that allows them to accrue Goblin Debt.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by infastructure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T15:21:33-08:00","id":1187359,"title":"","content":"Goblin Markets can exist outside the Hedge. A mage could end up shopping there and buying items or services.<br /> Contracts might only be useful if the Loophole is not to obscure.<br /> <br /> Hedge Denizen does not benefit the mage though. The Hedge is very harmful to mages. Staying outside the Hedge gives the Deprived condition, bad, but not crippeling. Getting some Goblin Contracts is nice, but underwhelming compared to Supernal magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 02-18-2018, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}